issue_context.body:
### Description

When casting an ImmutableArray to an IList, calls to IndexOf do not act as they do in other collections.  Other collections return -1 for items that are not found, regardless of their type.  ImmutableArray cast to IList then IndexOf is called will throw a NullReferenceException or InvalidCastException depending on the parameter passed in.
I originally found this when I noticed a Binding in WPF throwing an exception when bound to an ImmutableArray.  WPF was assuming that IndexOf on IList would always return -1 for a non-match.

### Reproduction Steps

Assuming the following Enum:
`enum States
{
    A,
    B
}`

The following code will show the problem:

    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        List<States> list = new List<States>(new[] { States.A, States.B });
        TestList(list);

        States[] array = new[] { States.A, States.B };
        TestList(list);

        ImmutableArray<States> imm = ImmutableArray.Create(new[] { States.A, States.B });
        TestList(imm);
    }

    private static void TestList(IList list)
    {
        list.IndexOf(States.A);
        list.IndexOf(null);
        list.IndexOf(new object());
    }

TestList on ImmutableArray throws a NullReferenceException when ilist.IndexOf(null) is called.  If that line is commented out, it will throw an InvalidCastException when ilist.IndexOf(new object()) is called.

### Expected behavior

I would expect IList.IndexOf to return -1 and not throw one of those exceptions regardless of the implementing type.

### Actual behavior

A NullReferenceException or an InvalidCastException are thrown, depending on whether null is passed as a parameter, or an invalid type is passed as a parameter.

### Regression?

_No response_

### Known Workarounds

_No response_

### Configuration

Version:  7.0
OS:  Windows 10
Arch:  X64
I doubt it is unique to this OS or machine architecture.

### Other information

This may be because at https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/a7f3df9b14d896cda708e2d22f35165737646769/src/libraries/System.Collections.Immutable/src/System/Collections/Immutable/ImmutableArray_1.cs#L1211 the passed in parameter is directly cast to the type in the collection.
